<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, and defect pair annihilation — MorphoEval overall 91.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) remediated evaluation of `2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py` (consensus score 91.4/100, up from 52.8/100 in Pass 1). The remediated script implements a 2D multi-dislocation eikonal step-flow and complex order-parameter solver (`simulate_chiral_dislocation_terrace_2d`, L183-305) plus 3D bivalve sheet vs gastropod tower nacre architectures (`simulate_nacre_architecture_3d`, L351-405), verifying all 4 chiral defect morphospace regimes (subcritical dipole annihilation control d=0.60 um <= 2*r_c -> 0 terraces, single screw spiral b_net=+1, supercritical Frank-Read target rings d=2.40 um > 2*r_c with b_net=0, and same-chirality double spiral b_net=+2 with halved pitch ratio 0.5000), collapses 12 empirical bivalve, gastropod, and cephalopod species onto the BCF law lambda_0 ≈ 18.9848*r_c (r=0.9999, slope=18.99), and segments 312 inter-lamellar mortar seams (h_0 = 0.5000 um, CV = 0.2933, aspect ratio = 3.2436) on the SHA-256-locked SEM mother-of-pearl specimen, backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems. Overall 91.4/100 (faithfulness 91.3, reproducibility 91.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit HEAD; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_comparison.png: rendered output of 2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py at HEAD, image/png, 1412174 B, 2224×1495 px, artifact_sha256 a86ba495f00ab18584495b2c9e61aa9c452bb1ebebdb24c5ef65f9dc761dc2de (sha256 a86ba495f00ab18584495b2c9e61aa9c452bb1ebebdb24c5ef65f9dc761dc2de), spec_fingerprint 4c231c8398be9a26483bc4175fe15077a90c9e9b18a12deaf2c2e4265b43d447. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 4c231c8398be9a26483bc4175fe15077a90c9e9b18a12deaf2c2e4265b43d447; artifact_sha256: a86ba495f00ab18584495b2c9e61aa9c452bb1ebebdb24c5ef65f9dc761dc2de; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_aragonite_tablets_specimen.jpg=e4c6590464523f21..., datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json=580b05d6121d9596..., datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/scout_manifest.json=6084a2ce133990fc...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2D multi-dislocation eikonal terrace solver to a 3D phase-field chitin-membrane perforation model (Cartwright & Checa 2007 Sec. 4) to resolve mineral bridge alignment across successive inter-lamellar sheets.",
        "remediation needed: Incorporate crystallographic aragonite twinning and crystallographic [100]/[010] step-velocity anisotropy into the spiral core polygonization." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.14e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

